  "confidence": 0.78,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["74LVC1G86 (root sheet, controller.kicad_sch)", "U1", "U4", "U8"],
      "pins": ["U1.22 (GPIO7)", "U4.5", "U8.1", "U8.6"],
      "nets": ["Tro1_XOR_A", "Tro1_XOR_B", "Tro1_XOR_Y"],
      "observed": "The root sheet contains a 74LVC1G86 XOR gate whose pins carry global labels Tro1_XOR_A (pin1), Tro1_XOR_B (pin2) and Tro1_XOR_Y (pin4). Tro1_XOR_A also appears on the ESP32 U1 at the GPIO7 row (mcu sheet), Tro1_XOR_B appears on the buck converter U8's FB/BST node (power sheet), and Tro1_XOR_Y appears on thermocouple U4 (thermocouples sheet). The spec describes no such gate and no Tro1_XOR_* nets anywhere.",
      "expected": "Per the spec the thermocouple channels are a plain shared SPI bus (SCK/SO + CS0-CS2) with U4 VCC tied to +3V3 and SCK tied to the ESP32, and the buck's FB pin is 'tied directly to +3V3'. No logic gate should sit in the SPI path or on the regulator feedback node.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Root sheet (controller.kicad_sch): 74LVC1G86 symbol with global labels Tro1_XOR_A, Tro1_XOR_B, Tro1_XOR_Y on pins 1/2/4"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "mcu sheet: 'Tro1_XOR_A' label on U1 GPIO7 row; power sheet: 'Tro1_XOR_B' on U8 FB/BST node; thermocouples sheet: 'Tro1_XOR' label on U4"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "SCK (pin 5) and SO (pin 7, tri-state/MISO) are common nets (SCK, SO) tied to all three ICs and to the ESP32 ... Power: V_{CC} (pin 4) -> +3V3 ... FB(1) is tied directly to +3V3"}
      ],
      "impact": "The XOR gate injects a logic output into the thermocouple U4 signal line and merges an MCU GPIO with the buck converter's feedback/soft-start node, corrupting SPI reads of the thermocouples and disturbing the 3.3 V regulation; this is not part of the intended architecture.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["U1"],
      "pins": ["U1.18 (GPIO3)", "U1.19 (GPIO4)", "U1.20 (GPIO5)", "U1.21 (GPIO6)", "U1.22 (GPIO7)"],
      "nets": ["CS0", "SCK", "CS1", "CS2", "Tro1_XOR_A"],
      "observed": "On the mcu sheet the SPI global labels are attached one GPIO lower than the spec states: CS0 on the GPIO3 row, SCK on the GPIO4 row, CS1 on the GPIO5 row, CS2 on the GPIO6 row, and the GPIO7 row (the spec's CS2 pin) instead carries Tro1_XOR_A.",
      "expected": "Spec: 'SPI2 on GPIO5/GPIO10, CS pins GPIO4/6/7' and 'SCK ... tied to ... ESP32 (U1 GPIO5/SCK ...); ... CS0/CS1/CS2, driven by ESP32 GPIO4/GPIO6/GPIO7 respectively'. SCK must be on GPIO5 and CS0/CS1/CS2 on GPIO4/GPIO6/GPIO7.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "mcu sheet right column of U1: CS0 aligned to '18 GPIO3', SCK to '19 GPIO4', CS1 to '20 GPIO5', CS2 to '21 GPIO6', Tro1_XOR_A to '22 GPIO7'"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "SCK ... tied to ... ESP32 (U1 GPIO5/SCK, GPIO10/SO). Each chip has its own independent chip-select ... driven by ESP32 GPIO4/GPIO6/GPIO7 respectively"}
      ],
      "impact": "The firmware's SCK/CS GPIOs no longer match the routed nets (SCK toggles the CS1 line, CS2 toggles the CS1 line, etc.), so none of the three MAX31855 channels can be clocked or selected correctly; the thermocouple sensing is broken.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build contains an undocumented 74LVC1G86 XOR gate with Tro1_XOR_A/B/Y nets that bridge an ESP32 GPIO, the buck converter's feedback/soft-start node, and thermocouple U4, and the SPI/CS labels on U1 are shifted one GPIO off from the spec (GPIO7 repurposed as the XOR input) - both deviate from the intended architecture and would corrupt thermocouple reads and the 3.3 V rail."
}

